---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy — Ed Chapman"
  description="Privacy on edwardchapman.co.uk: no analytics, no tracking, one functional cookie."
>
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p>
    This site has no analytics, tracking scripts, or accounts. Reading it leaves
    no record with me beyond the ordinary request logs Cloudflare processes to
    operate the site. The one cookie this site sets is functional and described
    below.
  </p>
  <p>
    When you use <a href="/ask">Ask about Ed's work</a>, your question is first
    checked against a short list of pre-written answers to common questions; if
    none matches, it is sent to Anthropic to generate an answer. Either way it
    is recorded in the site's operational logs so abuse of the assistant can be
    detected. Those logs expire automatically after a short period; answers are
    never stored, and there is no database or account system behind this site.
    Do not include personal or sensitive information in a question. To keep the
    assistant available to everyone, asking a question that reaches the model
    sets a signed cookie that counts how many questions your browser has asked
    in the past 24 hours. It contains only that count — no identifier and no
    tracking — and is sent only with Ask requests.
  </p>
  <p>
    Questions about any of this:
    <a href="mailto:ed@edwardchapman.co.uk">ed@edwardchapman.co.uk</a>.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
